  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kedgeree descended from the South Asian "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "khichri",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "khichri"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " and is one of the defining dishes of Anglo-Indian cooking. Smoked haddock is poached in milk, then flaked into spiced buttery rice with hard-boiled eggs. Use undyed smoked haddock; the dyed kind turns everything a garish orange."
          }
        ]
      },
